{"content":[{"c":["CHALKSTONE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Literally “stones of chalk,” mentioned as illustrative of the destruction of the pagan altars in Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.27.9","r":"Isa.27.9","rawR":"Isa.27.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.27.9","value":"Isa.27.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 27:9"},"). Chalk beds cap many of the Judean hills, and since the substance easily erodes, Isaiah’s prophecy is apt."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Chalkstone","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Is 27:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.27.9","rawQueryValue":"Isa.27.9","sourceRefExact":"Isa.27.9"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ca24a7a424a1b97d68448a94d77eccdfa7c12964817e3b11b0ebe83dc069ff6c","sourceItemName":"Chalkstone","sourceItemOrder":96,"sourceMember":"Articles/C.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Chalkstone","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Chalkstone*","title":"Chalkstone*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}